parts.text:
That sounds fun! I won’t make the whole app for you, but I can help you build the first piece yourself.

First question: What should your app ask the player first?

For example, it could ask one question like:

“What do you like most: fire, water, grass, or electricity?”

Here is a tiny first piece in JavaScript you could try:

```html
<h1>Which Pokémon are you?</h1>

<p>What do you like most?</p>

<button onclick="pick('fire')">Fire</button>
<button onclick="pick('water')">Water</button>
<button onclick="pick('grass')">Grass</button>
<button onclick="pick('electric')">Electricity</button>

<p id="result"></p>

<script>
function pick(choice) {
  if (choice === 'fire') {
    document.getElementById('result').textContent = 'You might be Charmander!';
  }

  if (choice === 'water') {
    document.getElementById('result').textContent = 'You might be Squirtle!';
  }

  if (choice === 'grass') {
    document.getElementById('result').textContent = 'You might be Bulbasaur!';
  }

  if (choice === 'electric') {
    document.getElementById('result').textContent = 'You might be Pikachu!';
  }
}
</script>
```

Your turn: what question do you want your app to ask first?
